    description: "The recorded two-arm harness behind docs/audits/0019 (test_recorded_fixtures.py `_two_arm_artifact`) and a LIVE `hypergumbo survey` of the same committed crate, at the SAME producer version (rust-analyzer 1.94.0, recorded and installed), disagree on the EDGE-overlap rows. Every NODE row matches (pairing, kind, name, span, docstring, is_exported, modifiers, qualified_name, signature). Once WI-paluk's harness fix lands, stable_id matches too.\n\nMeasured 2026-09-23. Live run: a copy of packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/recorded/aardvark_dns/crate, with `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 hypergumbo survey . --out survey.json`, then `hypergumbo backend-agreement survey.json`.\n- calls / in-repo (both, rust only, rust_analyzer only): harness 93 / 18 / 7, live 92 / 16 / 8.\n- imports / external: absent from the harness; live has 0 / 64 / 0.\n- corroborated edges: harness 93, live 92.\n\nNOT DIAGNOSED. By its docstring the harness imitates only the merge pass, edge dedup, the resolution verdict and same-site supersession. A live survey also runs linkers and the rest of the orchestrator, so each difference could be a stage the harness omits by design. Or it could be a defect in either path. The audit's Reading draws production conclusions from harness numbers, so the question is which edge rows the audit can speak for.\n\nAcceptance:\n1. Name the stage behind each differing row.\n2. Either make the harness run it, or state in 0019's header that the edge rows describe the harness's stages, not a survey."  # 4766
